Z||000000||maryjane||12-15-2001||02:21 AM||||I've got another computer with win95 on it. In the c:/windows/temp directory, there are a bunch of sub folders-all are just numbers:<BR>DE5E2E8C-EE-...<BR>and:<BR>ISTMP1.dir, ISTMP3.dir<BR>What are these? especially the first one.<BR>Also have a bunch of the following type files:<BR>AU_1175.tmp-----listed as a TAG file.<BR>What is a TAG file? I've always heard that anything in windows/temp directory can be safely deleted. Does this include the sub folders? Can they be deleted while windows is running or do I have to boot into a dos prompt? Can I delete EVERYTHING in the windows/temp directory? I really need an answer to each of these questions. Thanks<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 12-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||btoth||12-15-2001||02:25 PM||||You should have no problems deleting anything that's in a TEMP directory, unless <B>you</B> put stuff there that you want to keep.  Otherwise, it's just where programs toss things durring intalls or upgrades and they never clean up after themselves.||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||12-15-2001||04:08 PM||||Thanks Btoth, that's what I always heard. As far as putting stuff in temp to save, That's what that computer is for, to keep stuff on that I want off of this one. BTW if any of you see a mep####.tmp or mep####.exe file in your temp folder, it is put there by NIMDA A-0 virus. Mcafee stopped it on my email, so I read up on it a little.....||||reg||1
